            <div xml:id="d561">

                <pb facs="0551" n="539" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg539"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51A/869: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-10-12T17:00:00-04:00">October 12, 1943—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>527. You should inform Millspaugh at once that he should take no action until the
                    whole matter is thoroughly discussed through the Legation with the Department.
                    This is obviously a matter of the gravest importance and we are surprised that
                    Millspaugh should have reached any decision without a full and frank interchange
                    of views with the Department. This refers to your 989, October 11, 4 p.m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
